; incr.scm (future work) with + expanded, as basic blocks, called from the top level: (incr 0).
; + tests fixnum? (then fx+? with its overflow check), flonum?, and falls back to the generic ##+,
; as in polynomial-square.bbv. With intervals, x is exactly 0 in the entry of incr called by main.
function main()
M:  call incr(0) -> N
N:  return #res

function incr(x)
A:  if fixnum?(x) goto B else goto C
B:  r = fx+?(x, 1)
    if r goto R else goto D
R:  return r
C:  if flonum?(x) goto F else goto D
F:  return fl+(x, 1.0)
D:  return ##+(x, 1)
